Report gfxstream 3D resources' layout and export them on demand.

crosvm's display path (VirtioGpuScanout::import_resource_to_display) hands a
scanout resource to the Wayland compositor as a dma-buf, instead of reading it
back into a wl_shm buffer, when export_blob and resource3d_info both succeed.
For gfxstream, create_3d already exports the color buffer's memory but left
info_3d empty, so the lookup failed for every non-blob resource (the guest's
hwcomposer framebuffers) and the console always took the GPU-to-CPU copy. Fill
it from stream_renderer_resource_get_info (format and stride, no known
modifier: gfxstream's images are tiled host images whose layout the importer
has to take from the dma-buf itself), and let Rutabaga::export_blob ask the
component when no handle was cached at creation.

